---
import FeaturesLayout from '../../layouts/FeaturesLayout.astro';
const codeBlock =
  'bg-cdx-bg-alt/60 text-cdx-text overflow-x-auto rounded-lg p-3 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed';
const inlineCode = 'text-cdx-text bg-cdx-bg-alt rounded px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.85em]';
---

<FeaturesLayout
  currentSlug="routing"
  title="Routing — compodocx"
  description="How compodocx routes its static SPA — clean paths by default, hash mode for sub-paths without rewrite rules."
>
  <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary text-lg">
    The output is a static SPA. A small router handles deep links, scroll restoration, and page
    transitions without shipping a framework runtime.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-cdx-text text-xl font-semibold mt-12 first:mt-0">Sub-path hosting</h2>
  <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary">
    For GitHub Pages project sites, S3 prefixes, or any nested host, set the base path. compodocx
    rewrites every internal href and the search index URLs so deep links survive.
  </p>

  {/* prettier-ignore */}
  <pre class:list={codeBlock}><code>npx compodocx --basePath /my-project/</code></pre>

  <h2 class="text-cdx-text text-xl font-semibold mt-12 first:mt-0">Hash routing</h2>
  <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary">
    For environments without rewrite rules (some intranet hosts, file:// previews), hash-based
    routing keeps deep links working without server config.
  </p>

  {/* prettier-ignore */}
  <pre class:list={codeBlock}><code>npx compodocx --routingMode hash</code></pre>

  <h2 class="text-cdx-text text-xl font-semibold mt-12 first:mt-0">Scroll restoration</h2>
  <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary">
    Anchor scrolls account for the sticky NavBar height — no clicking
    <code class={inlineCode}>#api</code> and landing with the heading hidden behind the topbar. Back /
    forward navigation restores the prior scroll position.
  </p>
</FeaturesLayout>
